Description: Implements the Single-Index/Cox (SIC) mixture cure model
    proposed by Amico, Van Keilegom and Legrand (2019)
    <doi:10.1111/biom.12999>. The population survival function is
    written as S(t|x,z) = 1 - p(x) + p(x) * Su(t|z), where p(x) =
    g(gamma'x) is the incidence (probability of being uncured) modeled
    via a single-index structure with unknown link function g estimated
    nonparametrically using kernel smoothing (Nadaraya-Watson
    leave-one-out estimator), and Su(t|z) is the latency (conditional
    survival of the uncured subjects) modeled via a Cox proportional
    hazards model. Estimation is performed by maximum likelihood using
    an Expectation-Maximization (EM) algorithm. The bandwidth for the
    kernel estimator is selected at each EM iteration by likelihood
    cross-validation. The package includes functions for fitting the
    model, predicting incidence and survival for new observations,
    and computing prediction error.
